  <xs:complexType name="t_person_registration">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="ID">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:maxLength value="255" />
            <xs:minLength value="1" />
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="Password">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>
        UNODC suggests to use the below regular expression as a minimum level of complexity to enforce a strong password.
        This expression will enforce a  minimum of 8 chars with 1 uppercase, 1 lowercase, 1 number and 1 special character
        Please note that patterns used in the schema are Javascript regular expressions and may not appear valid in tools like Altova
        You can test your patterns at https://regex101.com - select Ecmascript from the regex flavour list on the left
						<xs:pattern value="^.*(?=.*\d)(?=.*[^a-zA-Z0-9])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*[a-z]).{8,}$" /></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:maxLength value="10" />
            <xs:minLength value="5" />
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="user_code">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:maxLength value="50" />
